  "description": "Overview: Artificial Arcade is a gaming hackathon focused on creativity, innovation, and game development. Teams design and develop innovative gaming experiences under time constraints. Encourages teamwork, technical skills, and problem-solving. Domains: Game Development Eligibility: Open to all students from a technical background. Inter-college participation allowed. Team Rules: Team-based participation only; no individual entries. Team size: 2-3 members. Inter-college and inter-department teams allowed. Format: Round 1: Resume Screening Teams shortlisted based on resume screening. Selected teams advance to Round 2. Round 2: Offline (24-Hour Hackathon) Dates: 23rd–24th October 2026. Teams develop and present their gaming projects. Food and refreshments provided. Top 10 teams qualify for the Grand Finale. Round 3: Grand Finale (8 Hours) Date: 30th October 2026. Top 10 teams compete in the final round. Rules & Regulations: Valid college ID required for verification. Project work must follow the respective round's time limits. Plagiarism and unauthorized copying are prohibited. Participants must follow the Code of Conduct. Judges’ and organizing committee’s decisions are final and binding. Event Date & Timeline: Round 1: Resume screening before the hackathon. Round 2: 23rd October 2026 – 24th October 2026 (24 hours). Round 3: 30th October 2026 (8 hours).",
